propose-3.pilot_plan:
ALREADY DONE (2026-09-28)
About 20k simulated episodes in /home/jovyan/dev/cbba-sota/pilots/trackD_integ (T1 world, list-scheduling planner):
- P2: consistency variants (CAS);
- P3: knowledge oracles (release, task status, teammate state, all);
- P4: dead reckoning (harmful) and the clamped snapshot;
- P5: global state beacons;
- P6: lease patience;
- P7: every method on the same lease, plus the staleness gate SG;
- P8: asymmetric scope HYB, local-write HYB2, regime gate HYB3.
Numbers: out/summary.txt, regenerated by summarize.py.

REMAINING 1-WEEK PILOT (dev only; 4 settings x 20 instances x 2 seeds)
- D1: Freeze the DX world.
  - Regression tests: arrival-order equals the env's decision-order at ideal links; FULL plan-following equals DynTaskEnv execute_by_route; the static reduction is bit-identical.
  - Plug in the state-start ALNS as the only planner, with an iteration-budgeted deterministic mode and per-event CPU accounting.
- D2: T2 channel: per-hop latency; GE and Rayleigh per CV_MRTA; byte budget; priority gossip. Cross-check against cbja/network.py on 5 small cases.
- D3: Re-measure the map with ALNS, at R/r_c in {2, 1, 0.75, 0.5}, leases tuned per method from the shared grid, for:
  - FULL;
  - CEN-RH with 3 fallbacks;
  - REP-v and REP-v+clamp;
  - HALO with theta in {0.5, 0.7, 0.9};
  - the REP-AO and REP-KO oracles.
- D4: Online baselines:
  - RL(g.) on beliefs, with a test that it reproduces DynTaskEnv rollouts at ideal links;
  - fixed greedy and OPEN;
  - a CBTA-lite reimplementation.
- D5: Factorial and knockouts at both primary ranges; ALNS budget sweep {0.05, 0.2, 0.5, 2} s per event.
- D6: Secondary stressors (RN3, R-B, Bernoulli 0.5, Rayleigh, 2 crash failures, beacon factor); message, byte and CPU accounting.
- D7: Decide against the kill criteria. Write docs/trackD-spec.md and freeze theta, leases and fallbacks.

KILL CRITERIA (dev, T2, ALNS planner)
- K1 no headroom: FULL is within 5% of the best link-limited baseline at 0.5 r_c. Drop the C3 method claim; keep the benchmark.
- K2 no fragmented win: HALO/CEN-RH upper 95% CI >= 0.97 at 0.5 r_c. Stop.
- K3 threshold loss: HALO/CEN-RH lower CI > 1.03 at 1.0 r_c after tuning theta. Keep only a regime-limited claim.
- K4 collapse: HALO is worse than REP-v+clamp by > 2% (CI above 1) at either range. The replicated solver becomes the method, reported as such.
- K5 planner does not carry online: ALNS beats list scheduling by < 3% at ideal links. Reframe C1-online.
- K6 compute: p95 re-plan CPU > 0.5 s at 50 tasks on 1 core.
- K7 RL anomaly: RL(g.) on beliefs lands within 10% of HALO. Investigate before anything else.
- K8 fragility: the conclusion flips within the lease or fallback grid. Report the sensitivity, then either restate the claim as holding over the grid or drop it.
